A||||5||btoth||New Fiero Store steering wheel||||2||
Z||000000||btoth||10-09-2001||09:51 PM||||Well at first I was discuraged by the fact that I had to mess with the rivits that hold the plastic ring for the horn button.  I think the Fiero Store should really include 4 small screws with nuts to use after you knock the rivits out.  Also, it is not just like the factory wheel.  I was under the impression from their write-up on their web site that yes, it was aftermarket, but that it was essentially a replica of the factory 3-spoke wheel.  It's a 13" wheel that is much "chunkier" than the original.  I like it, but it wasn't what I thought I was buying.  I plan on writing them an email, recomending that they "improve" their description of the wheel.  I'm also not quite sure if it is leather... doesn't feel or smell like leather... hmmm.  Basically I got a Grant wheel that my factory horn button fits on... for $150.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif">||||reg||2
Z||000001||California Kid||10-09-2001||09:58 PM||||I got one from them a little more than a year ago and it is a re-conditioned leather factory wheel that came with plastic collar riveted in place.  Sounds like they ran out of wheels to re-condition, got after market wheels, and didn't change the web site.||||reg||1
Z||000002||btoth||10-10-2001||09:10 AM||||I guess so, I remember when they had a core charge for your old wheel.  I like the new one... looks like it belongs in the car more than the factory one, but still.  I like to know what I'm paying for.  Oh well.||||reg||1
